  "term": "evolved mechanism",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, an evolved mechanism is the view of mind as a gradually developed functional system whose actions can become highly organized and even largely automatic through habit and training. It presents mental life as a subject for scientific study grounded in its development and relation to the organism, rather than needing speculative additions.",
